<title>POLAND: Volvo Bus Poland to produce 140 buses in 1997.</title>
<headline>Volvo Bus Poland to produce 140 buses in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Polish venture between Sweden's Volvo unit, Volvo Bus Corporation, and Finnish body-maker Carrus Oy, will produce 140 buses in Poland this year, the firm's marketing director said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;We plan to produce about 140 buses,&quot; Lars Forsbergh of Volvo Bus Poland told a news conference, adding that more than 50 of those buses will be exported to Denmark and Sweden.</p>
<p>Volvo Bus Poland also plans to start making tourist coaches in the second or third quarter of this year, Forsbergh said.</p>
<p>The firm started production in October 1996.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
